<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Minecraft Master Guide</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-dark: #121212;
            --bg-card: #1e1e1e;
            --accent-green: #55ff55;
            --accent-green-dark: #2d862d;
            --text-light: #f0f0f0;
            --text-muted: #aaa;
            --border-color: #333;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
        }

        body {
            background-color: var(--bg-dark);
            color: var(--text-light);
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        header {
            background-color: #050505;
            border-bottom: 3px solid var(--accent-green-dark);
            padding: 2rem 1rem;
            text-align: center;
        }

        header h1 {
            color: var(--accent-green);
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px #000;
        }

        header p {
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        nav {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            background-color: #1a1a1a;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 100;
        }

        .nav-btn {
            background: none;
            border: none;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
            font-size: 1rem;
            font-weight: bold;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .nav-btn:hover {
            color: var(--accent-green);
            background-color: #252525;
        }

        .nav-btn.active {
            color: var(--accent-green);
            border-bottom: 3px solid var(--accent-green);
            background-color: var(--bg-card);
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1100px;
            margin: 2rem auto;
            padding: 0 1rem;
        }

        .tab-content {
            display: none;
        }

        .tab-content.active {
            display: block;
        }

        .grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
            gap: 1.5rem;
            margin-top: 1.5rem;
        }

        .card {
            background-color: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            transition: transform 0.2s ease;
        }

        .card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-4px);
            border-color: var(--accent-green-dark);
        }

        .card h3 {
            color: var(--accent-green);
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }

        code {
            background-color: #000;
            color: #ff5555;
            padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-family: monospace;
            font-size: 0.9em;
        }

        .search-bar {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 0.8rem;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            background-color: #000;
            color: #fff;
            font-size: 1rem;
        }

        ul {
            margin-left: 1.2rem;
            margin-top: 0.5rem;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 2rem;
            background-color: #050505;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin-top: 3rem;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Minecraft Knowledge Hub</h1>
        <p>Your ultimate companion guide for commands, blocks, structures, and automated farms.</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <button class="nav-btn active" onclick="openTab(event, 'commands')">Commands</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" onclick="openTab(event, 'blocks')">Blocks & Uses</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" onclick="openTab(event, 'structures')">Structures</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" onclick="openTab(event, 'farms')">Material Farms</button>
    </nav>

    <div class="container">

        <!-- COMMANDS TAB -->
        <section id="commands" class="tab-content active">
            <h2>Essential Commands</h2>
            <p>Commands allow you to alter the world, manage inventory, and change game rules.</p>
            <br>
            <input type="text" id="commandSearch" class="search-bar" onkeyup="filterCards('commands')" placeholder="Search commands...">
            
            <div class="grid">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3><code>/tp [target] [destination]</code></h3>
                    <p>Teleports a player or entity to a specific location or another player.</p>
                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> <code>/tp @p ~ ~10 ~</code> (Teleports you 10 blocks up)</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3><code>/give [player] [item] [amount]</code></h3>
                    <p>Gives a specified player an item in the requested quantity.</p>
                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> <code>/give @p diamond 64</code></p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3><code>/gamerule [rule] [value]</code></h3>
                    <p>Modifies core gameplay mechanics in your world.</p>
                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> <code>/gamerule keepInventory true</code></p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3><code>/locate structure [name]</code></h3>
                    <p>Displays the coordinates of the nearest specified structure.</p>
                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> <code>/locate structure village</code></p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3><code>/time set [day|night|number]</code></h3>
                    <p>Changes the time of day in the world cycle.</p>
                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> <code>/time set day</code></p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3><code>/fill [x1 y1 z1] [x2 y2 z2] [block]</code></h3>
                    <p>Fills a specified 3D area with a chosen block type.</p>
                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> <code>/fill ~-2 ~-1 ~-2 ~2 ~-1 ~2 stone</code></p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- BLOCKS TAB -->
        <section id="blocks" class="tab-content">
            <h2>Key Blocks & Their Purposes</h2>
            <p>Understand special functional blocks to improve crafting, building, and survival.</p>
            
            <div class="grid">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Crafting & Utility Blocks</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Crafter:</strong> Automated crafting block powered by Redstone.</li>
                        <li><strong>Anvil:</strong> Used for repairing items, combining enchantments, and naming objects.</li>
                        <li><strong>Enchanting Table:</strong> Enhances tools, armor, and weapons using Lapis Lazuli.</li>
                        <li><strong>Brewing Stand:</strong> Brews potions using Water Bottles and Blaze Powder fuel.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Redstone Components</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Observer:</strong> Detects block update changes and outputs a Redstone pulse.</li>
                        <li><strong>Hopper:</strong> Transfers items between containers or collects dropped items.</li>
                        <li><strong>Piston / Sticky Piston:</strong> Pushes (and pulls) blocks when activated by Redstone.</li>
                        <li><strong>Comparator:</strong> Measures inventory fullness or compares Redstone signal strengths.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Workstation Blocks</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Lectern:</strong> Allows multiple players to read a book; assigns Librarian job to villager.</li>
                        <li><strong>Blast Furnace:</strong> Smelts ores and metals twice as fast as a standard furnace.</li>
                        <li><strong>Smoker:</strong> Cooks food items twice as fast as a normal furnace.</li>
                        <li><strong>Stonecutter:</strong> Simplifies stone block crafting recipes without material waste.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- STRUCTURES TAB -->
        <section id="structures" class="tab-content">
            <h2>World Structures & Exploration</h2>
            <p>Key naturally generating structures and the valuable resources found inside them.</p>

            <div class="grid">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Overworld Structures</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Villages:</strong> Safe havens containing resources, beds, and trading options.</li>
                        <li><strong>Ancient City:</strong> Deep dark ruins containing Swift Sneak enchantments and Wardens.</li>
                        <li><strong>Ocean Monument:</strong> Underwater structure guarded by Guardians; contains Gold Blocks and Sponge.</li>
                        <li><strong>Woodland Mansion:</strong> Rare forest building housing Evokers (for Totems of Undying).</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Nether Structures</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Nether Fortress:</strong> Essential structure containing Nether Wart and Blaze Rods.</li>
                        <li><strong>Bastion Remnant:</strong> Piglin stronghold rich in Gold, Ancient Debris, and Pigstep music discs.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>End Structures</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Stronghold:</strong> Underground structure housing the End Portal frame.</li>
                        <li><strong>End Cities:</strong> Floating towers in the outer End islands; contain Elytra and Shulker Shells.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- FARMS TAB -->
        <section id="farms" class="tab-content">
            <h2>Material & Automation Farms</h2>
            <p>Popular farm designs to maximize resource gathering efficiency.</p>

            <div class="grid">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Iron Golem Farm</h3>
                    <p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong> 3 Villagers, 1 Zombie, Water, Lava, Hoppers, Chests.</p>
                    <p><strong>How it works:</strong> Trapping a Zombie near villagers frightens them into spawning an Iron Golem. Lava kills the golem, and hoppers collect the iron ingots into chests.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Automatic Sugarcane / Bamboo Farm</h3>
                    <p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong> Sugarcane, Water, Pistons, Observers, Redstone, Hopper System.</p>
                    <p><strong>How it works:</strong> Observers detect when the crop grows 3 blocks tall, triggering pistons to break the top two blocks without removing the base plant.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Mob XP & Drop Tower</h3>
                    <p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong> Solid blocks, Water buckets, Trapdoors, Hoppers, Slabs.</p>
                    <p><strong>How it works:</strong> Spawns mobs in a dark overhead chamber. Water currents push them down a 22-block drop shaft, leaving them with minimal HP for easy manual killing and XP gathering.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Gold & XP Farm (Nether)</h3>
                    <p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong> Netherrack, Magma blocks, Turtle Eggs, Trapdoors, Hoppers.</p>
                    <p><strong>How it works:</strong> Built above the Nether roof. Zombified Piglins are lured toward turtle eggs, falling into a collection drop where they yield massive amounts of Gold and XP.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>Minecraft Guide Homepage &copy; Created for Minecrafters everywhere.</p>
    </footer>

    <script>
        function openTab(evt, tabName) {
            let contents = document.getElementsByClassName("tab-content");
            for (let i = 0; i < contents.length; i++) {
                contents[i].classList.remove("active");
            }

            let buttons = document.getElementsByClassName("nav-btn");
            for (let i = 0; i < buttons.length; i++) {
                buttons[i].classList.remove("active");
            }

            document.getElementById(tabName).classList.add("active");
            evt.currentTarget.classList.add("active");
        }

        function filterCards(tabId) {
            let input = document.getElementById('commandSearch');
            let filter = input.value.toLowerCase();
            let container = document.getElementById(tabId);
            let cards = container.getElementsByClassName('card');

            for (let i = 0; i < cards.length; i++) {
                let cardText = cards[i].innerText || cards[i].textContent;
                if (cardText.toLowerCase().indexOf(filter) > -1) {
                    cards[i].style.display = "";
                } else {
                    cards[i].style.display = "none";
                }
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
